# Bilingual FR / US English (Process)

Every user-facing change in Process must work in **French (FR)** and **US English (EN)**.

## App (Swift / iOS)

### API

- **UI copy**: `AppCopy.t("…", en: "…")` — French first, English second.
- **Nonisolated** (catalogs, notifications, default args, Shared): `AppCopy.tSync("…", en: "…")`.
- **CTAs**: reuse `AppCopy.continueCTA`, `AppCopy.close`, `AppCopy.settings`, etc. when they fit.
- **Branding**: `AppBranding.replacingProcess` runs inside `AppCopy` — do not bypass it with raw `"Process"` hacks.

### Language source

- Product language = `ProcessAppLanguage` (`process.app.language` in UserDefaults).
- **Never** use `Locale.current` or `NSLocalizedString` for product copy.
- **Shared / widgets / Live Activity**: use `ProcessSharedLanguage.t(_:en:)` (reads the same UserDefaults key + device fallback).

### Checklist before finishing a Swift change

1. No bare `Text("…")` / `Button("…")` / `navigationTitle("…")` with words (numbers, `%`, `ml`, emojis OK).
2. No French-only strings in models, catalogs, notifications, accessibility labels.
3. No English string passed as the **French** argument to `AppCopy.t`.
4. Dynamic strings: interpolate inside both FR and EN versions.
5. New Shared copy → extend `ProcessHydrationCopy` or `ProcessSharedLanguage`, not duplicate logic.

### Examples

```swift
// ❌ BAD
Text("Continuer")
Text("Streak")
title: "Repas debloat"

// ✅ GOOD
Text(AppCopy.t("Continuer", en: "Continue"))
Text(AppCopy.t("Série", en: "Streak"))
title: AppCopy.tSync("Repas debloat", en: "Debloat meal")
```

```swift
// ❌ BAD — English in FR slot
AppCopy.t("Time to drink", en: "Time to drink")

// ✅ GOOD
ProcessSharedLanguage.t("C'est l'heure de boire", en: "Time to drink")
```

## Website (`website/`)

- User-facing JS copy: `appCopy("…", "…")` from `website/src/features/app-copy.js`.
- Detect language via `prefersEnglish()` (browser `navigator.languages`, same FR/en logic as the app).
- Static HTML fallback (FR) is OK if `get-app-mount.js` or the page mount overwrites copy on load.
- Referral/share payloads must include both locales in `buildReferralShareText`.

## When adding a feature

Ship **both locales in the same PR** — not a follow-up. If copy is provisional, still add EN placeholders; never leave FR-only user text.

## Review triggers (grep before merge)

- `Text("` with letters after the quote in Swift
- `title: "` / `detail: "` with French prose in catalogs
- `Locale.current` for copy (not formatting)
- Website strings assigned without `appCopy`
